WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.363
First: production's pre-flight
fails P F oh seven.

3
00:00:06.363 --> 00:00:07.462
What does that mean?

4
00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:08.688
The answer is b.

5
00:00:08.688 --> 00:00:13.638
The test stage's evidence doesn't pass its
stage check, so production can't start.

6
00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:15.848
P F oh seven runs in production only,

7
00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:20.499
and it's the guard against deploying
to production before test has passed.

8
00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:24.625
Second: why does production route
as a dry run for its first week?

9
00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:25.850
The answer is b.

10
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.337
So duplicate or misrouted
tasks don't reach the queue.

11
00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:33.906
The service desk works from the payloads
by hand, and sending is turned on only

12
00:00:33.906 --> 00:00:38.474
after the change manager approves, with
the settings flag and the send switch.

13
00:00:38.474 --> 00:00:40.902
The module page has three more questions,

14
00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:43.460
each linked to the
section that answers it.
